# TypeScript library conventions

## Modules

- Use ESM imports with **`.js` extensions** in relative paths (Node ESM resolution):

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
import { Cue } from './cue.js';

// ❌ BAD
import { Cue } from './cue';
```

- Strict TypeScript; avoid widening public types unnecessarily
- Private state uses `#field` private class fields

## Fluent API

Public mutators return `this` for chaining:

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
setText(text: string): this {
    this.#text = text;
    return this;
}
```

## Segments

- New segment kinds extend `Segment` and implement `toString`, `toJSON`, `valid`, and typically `static fromString`
- Set `_type` as a string literal (`'cue' | 'region' | 'style' | 'header' | 'comment'`)
- Re-export new public types from `src/segments/index.ts` and `src/index.ts` when they are part of the API

## Errors

- Add domain errors under `src/errors/` as `export default class … extends Error`
- Re-export from `src/errors/index.ts`
- Prefer throwing these over generic `Error` for parse/validation failures

## Formatting

- Prettier: 4-space indent, single quotes, semicolons, trailing commas, printWidth 80
